@startuml Sequence_Auth_JWT
!theme plain
autonumber

actor "Usuario" as User
participant "Browser/Client" as Client
participant "Flask API\n(/api/auth/login)" as API
participant "AuthService" as AuthService
participant "User Model" as UserModel
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

User -> Client: Ingresa credenciales\n(username, password)
activate Client

Client -> API: POST /api/auth/login\n{username, password}
activate API

API -> AuthService: validate_credentials(username, password)
activate AuthService

AuthService -> UserModel: query.filter_by(username=username)
activate UserModel

UserModel -> DB: SELECT * FROM user\nWHERE username = ?
activate DB
DB --> UserModel: user_record
deactivate DB

UserModel --> AuthService: User object
deactivate UserModel

AuthService -> AuthService: bcrypt.check_password_hash(\nuser.password_hash,\npassword)

alt Password válido
    AuthService -> AuthService: generate_access_token(user)
    AuthService -> AuthService: generate_refresh_token(user)
    
    AuthService --> API: {access_token, refresh_token,\nuser_data}
    deactivate AuthService
    
    API --> Client: 200 OK\n{\n  "access_token": "eyJ...",\n  "refresh_token": "eyJ...",\n  "user": {...}\n}
    deactivate API
    
    Client --> User: Login exitoso\n(guarda tokens en localStorage)
    deactivate Client
    
else Password inválido
    AuthService --> API: ValueError("Invalid credentials")
    deactivate AuthService
    
    API --> Client: 401 Unauthorized\n{"error": "Invalid credentials"}
    deactivate API
    
    Client --> User: Error de autenticación
    deactivate Client
end

note right of AuthService
  **Validación**
  - bcrypt con 12 rounds
  - Tokens JWT con expiración
  - Access: 15 min
  - Refresh: 30 días
end note

@enduml
